== 1. Survey method (owner request: "every file, line and code achieves its purpose; everything real")
a) Simulation markers in the live path (mock/fake/simulate/placeholder/TODO in server.py and
   agent_civilization outside specialists): none left in runtime code (removed in earlier phases).
b) Import reachability from server.py/run.py by AST — raw/41_r100_reachability_survey.log
   (script embedded verbatim). Not reachable from the live path:
   - agent_civilization/agents/executors/data_worker.py (96 lines) — no importer anywhere, tests included (grep rc=1)
   - agent_civilization/communication, runtime, utils — packages whose only file is a 0-byte __init__.py
   - agos_kernel/agent_production/* (20+531+338+451 = 1,340 lines) — tests only (D-032/D-033 deferred wiring)
   -> registered as R-104 and R-103 (proposed). Wording: "not connected to the verified run path", not "dead".
c) Reading each handler of real_dispatcher.py against its claim -> R-102 (proposed):
   _builder answers "N build action(s) queued" with no queue; _architect returns the same 5 layers for any input;
   _code_generator only parses; _designer derives a palette from a SHA-256 of the text; _analyst counts words for
   non-numeric goals; _modifier only collapses whitespace.
d) web/ never sends X-API-Key (grep of web/src: only the external agent's own api_key field) -> R-101 (ready).
e) Live probe of the default (open) mode — section 2. This was the critical finding and is fixed by R-100.

